{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetQAmUiUXr3PytvxxC9Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository uses:**\n- Errors thrown as `ApiException` subclasses from controllers; `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts to `ApiError` response\n- `ErrorCode` enum defines all machine-readable error codes \n- Tests verify both HTTP status *and* error body structure (not just status)\n- `ResourceNotFoundException` → 404, `ConflictException` → 409\n- In-memory storage with `ConcurrentHashMap`\n- Endpoints return `ResponseEntity` with status codes\n\n**Affected files (cannot be avoided):**\n1. `Order.kt` — add `status` field and `OrderStatus` enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` — add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — add method to find shipments by `orderId`\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — check for cancelled order when creating shipment\n5. `ApiError.kt` — add error code for forbidden cancellation\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — test cancel endpoint\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — test shipment rejection for cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Thread safety: concurrent cancel calls on same order could race on shipment status checks\n- Atomicity: cancelling shipments after order status update could leave order in inconsistent state\n- Existing tests break if Order serialization changes (tests expect certain fields)\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone — requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status` field to `Order` data class and create `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` that:\n   - Returns 404 if order not found\n   - Returns 409 if any shipment is `CONFIRMED` (throws `ConflictException`)\n   - Moves order to `CANCELLED` and cancels all `CREATED` shipments, returns 200 if order was `ACTIVE`\n   - Returns 200 with no changes if order already `CANCELLED`\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add method `findByOrderIdForUpdate()` or similar to support transactional reads, though in-memory store makes this simpler — use synchronized block for atomicity.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments by order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In `create()` method, check if order exists and is not `CANCELLED`. If `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with new error code.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to `ErrorCode` enum.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancel active order → 200, order now `CANCELLED`\n   - Cancel already cancelled order → 200, no change (idempotent)\n   - Cancel with confirmed shipment → 409, nothing changes\n   - Cancel nonexistent order → 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for:\n   - Create shipment for cancelled order → 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\n- *Create a new `OrderService` class*: The existing architecture uses repositories directly in controllers, and the requirement fits that pattern. Adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring.\n- *Use `@Transactional` annotation*: In-memory store doesn't need Spring transactions. Explicit locking via `synchronized` is simpler and more transparent.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | HTTP |\n|------|------|-------|----------|------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | order, shipments by order | order status→CANCELLED, CREATED shipments→CANCELLED | updated order | 200 |\n| Cancel CANCELLED order | order, shipments by order | (none) | order as-is | 200 |\n| Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment | order, shipments by order | (none) | error | 409 |\n| Cancel nonexistent order | (order lookup fails) | (none) | error | 404 |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | order | (none) | error | 409 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n| Test | File | Coverage |\n|------|------|----------|\n| Cancel active order returns 200, order CANCELLED, CREATED shipments cancelled | OrderControllerTest | active→cancelled transition |\n| Cancel already-cancelled order returns 200, nothing changes | OrderControllerTest | idempotency |\n| Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409, all-or-nothing | OrderControllerTest | conflict + atomicity |\n| Cancel nonexistent order returns 404 | OrderControllerTest | 404 case |\n| Create shipment for nonexistent order succeeds (baseline) | ShipmentControllerTest | existing behavior |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409 | ShipmentControllerTest | shipment rejection |\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by modifying the Order model to add the status field:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":303,"cache_read_input_tokens":25389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":303},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2ce1314-9603-4df1-b319-9a211cd47982","uuid":"37ad030b-c48e-4751-a026-2033b316c806","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:15:24.996Z","request_id":"req_011CetQAko2oSay6oBehLxJa"}
