t — added `findByOrderId()` method to query shipments by order for cancellation\n- ShipmentController.kt — added check to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders with 409 response\n- ApiError.kt — added `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt — added 8 tests: active order cancellation, idempotency, 404 for unknown, 409 for CONFIRMED, CREATED shipment cascading cancellation, mixed statuses, CANCELLED shipment handling\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 3 tests: non-existent order baseline, CANCELLED order rejection, ACTIVE order success\n\nTests:\n- Newly created orders have ACTIVE status\n- Cancelling ACTIVE order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n- Cancelling already-CANCELLED order returns 200, no changes (idempotent)\n- Cancelling non-existent order returns 404 with error envelope\n- Cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409, all-or-nothing (no changes)\n- Cancelling order cancels all CREATED shipments\n- Creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409 with error envelope\n- Creating shipment for non-existent order succeeds (baseline preserved)\n- Creating shipment for ACTIVE order succeeds (baseline preserved)\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` from sample-service directory completed with BUILD SUCCESS. All 24 tests passed (12 order tests, 8 shipment tests, 3 customer tests, 1 app test). Existing tests (4 order baseline + 5 shipment baseline) all pass. No regressions.\n\nNot done: Nothing. All acceptance criteria met, all requirements implemented, all tests passing, no unrelated changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":45871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e